cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these graphs, proofs or programs, please cite them as below, together with the earlier claims and papers listed in README.md."
type: dataset
title: "Erdős Problem #552: R(C4, K_{1,39}) = 46 and R(C4, K_{1,51}) = 59"
abstract: "Independent proofs of R(C4, K_{1,39}) = 46 and R(C4, K_{1,51}) = 59: the lower-bound graphs with Lean 4 proofs (core library, decide), the upper-bound counting arguments, two separately written SAT encodings of the case analysis, and the SHA-256 of every formula and LRAT certificate."
